    family-names: "Moya-Mendez"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine"

version: "1.0.2"
date-released: "2026-11-14"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-nhd-val-report"
url: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/pad-amp-nhd-val-report"

license: GPL-2.0-only

abstract: >
  The companion repository that renders the Word manuscript tables and figures for
  the pad-amp-nhd-val study from aggregate result artifacts alone. It has no
  database connection and no access to patient-level data: it reads only the
  small-cell-suppressed CSV artifacts written by the analysis repository, so the
  rendered report can be reproduced from an approved results export without
  access to the source CDM.
  Funding: Research reported in this publication was supported by the National
  Center For Advancing Translational Sciences of the National Institutes of Health
  under Award Number K12TR005435. The content is solely the responsibility of the
  authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the National
  Institutes of Health.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - external validation
  - risk score
  - non-home discharge
  - amputation
  - reproducible reporting
  - R

